+# ERT v0.1 — endpoint model-error and drift budgets
+
+For a target eta in the frozen PET tube, static gauge/species-phase invariant Hamiltonian errors with generic gradient bound nu and centered Hessian bound beta preserve all-time trapping when nu+eta beta<=N eta^3/12800. The original quartic barrier and initial modulus remain valid.
+
+On zero Gauss, a compact invariant minimizing set exists and is stable as a set. Its distance is bounded by the largest nonnegative root of c r^3-beta r/2-nu=0, at most eta/2; purely centered errors give sqrt(beta/(2c))<=eta/4. Cube-root and square-root exponents are demonstrated by exact scalar normal forms. An admitted uniform stiffness increase shows that trapping does not preserve nominal-orbit stability.
+
+Time dependence additionally needs a cumulative gradient-variation budget. Typed kinetic, magnetic, common/residual hopping and site-detuning limits share one sufficient inequality. Complex loop readouts have state error <21eta, with a separate instrument reserve; readout proximity does not certify preparation distance.
+
+Twenty-four exact algebraic checks, five rational budget examples, four numerical matrix-gradient/readout fixtures and eight visually checked PDF pages. Frozen PET support is inherited, not newly counted interval evidence. Development, no registry entry; independent review pending; physical promotion 0. No unique shifted orbit, attraction, physical calibration or empirical data analysis.
